Goal

Make three related product changes:

1. A true tie at the end of overtime.
If overtime expires and both sides have exactly the same score and the same knockback value—called Launch Point in this repository—the match must end in a tie. It must no longer silently restart a fresh battle.

2. Quick Battle gets a Regular Play / Custom Play choice.
When the player selects Quick Battle on the existing Select Mode screen, open a modal dialog with exactly two playable choices:

Custom Play
Regular Play

Do not immediately advance to Select Difficulty until one of those choices is selected.

3. Custom Play lets the player choose the CPU fighter, while Regular Play skips CPU and stage selection.

The resulting Quick Battle flows should be:

Home → Play → Select Mode → Quick Battle → Regular Play dialog choice → Select Difficulty → Select Fighter → Battle

For Regular Play, when the player confirms their fighter, automatically choose a random playable CPU fighter and a random normal battle stage, then start the Battle immediately. This intentionally skips the new Select CPU step and the existing Select Stage step.

The Custom Play flow should be:

Home → Play → Select Mode → Quick Battle → Custom Play dialog choice → Select Difficulty → Select Fighter → Select CPU → Select Stage → Battle

Custom Play therefore adds a new CPU fighter selection step immediately after Select Fighter.

Watch Mode and Practice Ground must remain functionally unchanged.

