Acceptance criteria

1. Clicking Quick Battle opens a modal with Custom Play and Regular Play instead of immediately entering Select Difficulty.
2. Escape/Back dismisses that modal without choosing either option and restores focus to Quick Battle.
3. Regular Play follows Mode → Difficulty → Fighter → Battle.
4. Regular Play automatically chooses one valid playable CPU fighter and one valid MAPS stage.
5. Regular Play never selects Practice Ground or an unavailable fighter.
6. Regular Play’s Restart and Rematch preserve the already chosen random CPU and stage.
7. Custom Play follows Mode → Difficulty → Fighter → CPU → Stage → Battle.
8. Custom Play’s CPU screen uses the existing roster architecture and stores a CPU fighter independently from the player fighter.
9. Quick Battle can run Player 1 and CPU as two different fighter definitions while preserving player/CPU controller roles.
